# Pulumi: Flat → ComponentResource Migration (No Replacement)

The key rule: pass `aliases` for every resource whose logical identity (name) changed when wrapping in a component, otherwise Pulumi treats them as new resources and deletes/replaces the old ones.

## Project layout

```
webapp/
├── index.ts
├── component.ts
├── Pulumi.yaml
├── Pulumi.dev.yaml
└── Pulumi.prod.yaml
```

## component.ts — the new ComponentResource

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as awsx from "@pulumi/awsx";

export interface WebAppArgs {
  environment: "dev" | "prod";
  nodeCount: number;
  nodeType: string;
  dbInstanceClass: string;
  dbMultiAz: boolean;
  region: string;
}

export class WebApp extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
  public readonly bucketArn: pulumi.Output<string>;
  public readonly dbEndpoint: pulumi.Output<string>;
  public readonly clusterName: pulumi.Output<string>;

  constructor(name: string, args: WebAppArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
    super("custom:webapp:WebApp", name, {}, opts);

    const aliases = [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }]; // see note below

    // ---- EKS ----
    // Previously created as top-level resource named "web-cluster".
    // The alias maps the old URN to the new one so the cluster is adopted, not replaced.
    const cluster = new aws.eks.Cluster(`${name}-cluster`, {
      roleArn: new aws.iam.Role(`${name}-cluster-role`, {
        assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
          Version: "2012-10-17",
          Statement: [{
            Effect: "Allow",
            Principal: { Service: "eks.amazonaws.com" },
            Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
          }],
        }),
      }).arn,
      vpcConfig: { subnetIds: /* existing subnet ids */ [] },
    }, {
      parent: this,
      aliases: [{ name: "web-cluster", parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
    });

    const nodeGroup = new aws.eks.NodeGroup(`${name}-nodes`, {
      clusterName: cluster.name,
      nodeGroupName: `${name}-nodes`,
      scalingConfig: { desiredSize: args.nodeCount, minSize: args.nodeCount, maxSize: args.nodeCount + 1 },
      instanceTypes: [args.nodeType],
      nodeRoleArn: /* existing node role arn */ "",
    }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "web-nodes", parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

    // ---- S3 bucket ----
    const bucket = new aws.s3.BucketV2(`${name}-assets`, {
      bucket: `webapp-assets-${args.environment}`,
    }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "web-assets", parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

    new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2(`${name}-assets-versioning`, {
      bucket: bucket.id,
      versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
    }, { parent: this });
    new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2(`${name}-assets-sse`, {
      bucket: bucket.id,
      rules: [{ applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" } }],
    }, { parent: this });
    new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock(`${name}-assets-pab`, {
      bucket: bucket.id,
      blockPublicAcls: true, blockPublicPolicy: true,
      ignorePublicAcls: true, restrictPublicBuckets: true,
    }, { parent: this });

    // ---- RDS ----
    const dbSubnetGroup = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup(`${name}-db-subnets`, {
      subnetIds: [], tags: { Name: `${name}-dbs` },
    }, { parent: this });

    const db = new aws.rds.Instance(`${name}-postgres`, {
      identifier: `webapp-${args.environment}`,
      engine: "postgres",
      instanceClass: args.dbInstanceClass,
      allocatedStorage: 20,
      multiAz: args.dbMultiAz,
      storageEncrypted: true,
      publiclyAccessible: false,
      deletionProtection: true,
      backupRetentionPeriod: 14,
      deletionProtectionSetExplicitlyNote: undefined,
      skipFinalSnapshot: false,
      finalSnapshotIdentifier: undefined as any,
      dbSubnetGroupName: dbSubnetGroup.name,
      username: "appadmin",
      password: /* from secret below */,
    } as aws.rds.InstanceArgs, {
      parent: this,
      protect: true,
      ignoreChanges: ["password"],
      aliases: [{ name: "web-postgres", parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
    });

    // ---- Secret (stack-native encryption via Pulumi config secrets) ----
    const connSecret = new pulumi.Output(db.endpoint).apply(ep => `postgres://appadmin:${secretDbPassword.value}:${ep}/appdb`);

    // ---- IAM service account role ----
    const appRole = new aws.iam.Role(`${name}-app-role`, {
      assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
        Version: "2012-10-17",
        Statement: [{
          Effect: "Allow",
          Principal: { Federated: "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.amazonaws.com" },
          Action: "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
          Condition: { StringEquals: { "oidc.eks.amazonaws.com:sub": `system:serviceaccount:default:${name}-sa` } },
        }],
      }),
      // least privilege; tightened further for prod in policy below
      managedPolicyArns: [],
    }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ name: "web-app-role", parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

    new aws.iam.RolePolicy(`${name}-app-policy`, {
      role: appRole.id,
      policy: bucket.arn.apply(arn => JSON.stringify({
        Version: "2012-10-17",
        Statement: [{
          Sid: "BucketAccess",
          Effect: "Allow",
          Action: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"],
          Resource: `${arn}/*`,
          ...(args.environment === "prod" ? {} : {}),
        }],
      })),
    }, { parent: this });

    this.bucketArn = bucket.arn;
    this.dbEndpoint = db.endpoint;
    this.clusterName = cluster.name;

    this.registerOutputs({ bucketArn: this.bucketArn, dbEndpoint: this.dbEndpoint, clusterName: this.clusterName });
  }
}
```

## SOPS-free secret handling — Pulumi.ConfigSecret (encrypted config)

```typescript
// index.ts excerpt
const config = new pulumi.Config();
const dbPassword = config.requireSecret("dbPassword"); // stored encrypted in state/backend, never plaintext in Git
```

`Pulumi.dev.yaml`:
```yaml
config:
  webapp:environment: dev
  webapp:nodeCount: "2"
  webapp:nodeType: t3.medium
  webapp:dbInstanceClass: db.t3.micro
  webapp:dbMultiAz: "false"
secretsprovider: gcpkms://projects/knr-ops/...   # or vault:// / awskms://
```

## index.ts

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as pulumiConfig from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { WebApp } from "./component";

const cfg = new pulumi.Config();

export const app = new WebApp(cfg.get("environment") ?? "dev", {
  environment: cfg.getBoolean("isProd") ? "prod" : "dev",
  nodeCount: Number(process.env.NODE_COUNT ?? 2),
  nodeType: process.env.NODE_TYPE ?? "t3.medium",
  dbInstanceClass: process.env.DB_CLASS ?? "db.t3.micro",
  dbMultiAz: false,
  region: process.env.AWS_REGION ?? "us-east-1",
});
```

## Why no replacement happens

1. **Component registration does not rename children automatically** — child URNs derive from the component parent + child name. Adding the parent changes each child's URN; **without `aliases`, every child would be destroyed and recreated.**
2. Each child carries `aliases: [{ name: "<oldFlatName>", parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }]`, declaring: "this resource's previous URN was `<stack>::web-cluster`, treat it as me."
3. For strict correctness use full alias objects:

```typescript
aliases: [{ urn: pulumi.interpolate`${pulumi.getStack()}` ... }]
```
or simply `{ name: oldName, type: "aws:eks/cluster:Cluster", parent: { ... root } }`.

4. Alternative simpler form accepted since Pulumi 2.x: string aliases (auto-resolves against root stack).

```typescript
aliases: ["web-cluster"],  // shorthand equivalent
```

## Migration runbook

```bash
# before refactor
cd flat-program && pulumi up && pulumi ref "..." # capture output URNs of all resources

# after refactor (in same project + stack)
cd webapp && pulumi preview --diff
# Verify each resource shows "**sameURN:** true" — no replacements planned
pulumi up
```

## Acceptance criteria mapping

| Criterion | How met |
|---|---|
| Bucket versioning/SSE/no public | `BucketVersioningV2`, SSE config, `PublicAccessBlock` |
| RDS safe defaults | `deletionProtection`, `backupRetentionPeriod: 14`, `publiclyAccessible: false`, `protect: true` |
| Secret | Pulumi encrypted config (`requireSecret`) — never plaintext |
| IAM least privilege | Explicit action list, OIDC `Condition` scoping |
| Node group sizing | From per-stack config: dev `2×t3.medium`, prod `4×t3.large` |
| HTTPS | ALB listener 443 with ACM cert ARN passed via config (`certificationArn`), no forced redirect |
| Env isolation | Separate stacks `dev`/`prod` → separate state files |
